          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 38,
              "body": "```suggestion\r\nIPv4 packets with private destination addresses are routinely translated to IPv4 packets with global destination addresses in NAT44. \r\nSimilarly, an IPv6 packet with a destination address representing a private IPv4 address [RFC6052] can be translated to an IPv4 packet with a global destination address by NAT64 [RFC6146].\r\nIf a 464XLAT CLAT cannot translate a private IPv4 address to an IPv6 address using the NAT64 /96 prefix and that IPv4 address [RFC6052], then the packet may not be translated to an IPv4 packet with a global address by the 464XLAT PLAT (stateful NAT64). This changes the intent of the sender, and in so doing violates the end to end principle. \r\n```",
              "createdAt": "2025-11-19T18:37:37Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-11-19T18:37:37Z"
            }
          ]
        },
